<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27298" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŭtŭlentus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		2. lutum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>muddy</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sus,</span>”
				<i>bedaubed with mud</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 2, 2, 75</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">diluvio tellus lutulenta recenti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					1, 434</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amnis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Am. 3, 6, 95</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 9, 23, 13</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>besmeared</i> with
			ointment: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">et putri lutulenta de palaestra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					7, 67, 7</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Filthy, dirty, vile</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lenone istoc non lutum est lutulentius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Poen. 1, 1, 29</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scio ego, multos jam lucrum lutulentos homines
					reddidit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Capt. 2, 2, 76</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lutulente Caesonine,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Pis. 12, 27</span></i>
			: persona illa lutulenta, impura. <i><span class="en">id. Rosc.
				Com. 7, 20</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Pis.
					1, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">qui vexat lutulentā balnea
					turbā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					7, 131</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Of
			style, <i>muddy, turbid, impure</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(Lucilius) cum flueret lutulentus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 1, 4, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">at dixi fluere hunc lutulentum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1, 10, 50</span></i>
			.—Hence, * adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŭtŭlentē</span></b> , <i>impurely</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lotiolente dictum velut lutulente,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Non. 131, 32</span></i>
			.</div>
